  "note": "First election of the whole Londonderry Corporation (40 members) after proportional representation was abolished, on the restored wards; nominations closed Friday 5 January 1923. The Nationalists boycotted the election and no candidate was nominated for the West Ward (two aldermen, six councillors). The Returning Officer gave notice, dated 8 January 1923, that the ward's retiring aldermen and councillors were deemed re-elected (Derry Journal, 10 January 1923, p. 5); the Derry Journal of 8 January 1923, p. 6 names them as Aldermen Meenan and Conn Bradley and Councillors Carlin, Hegarty, Logue, M'Kernan, M'Clean and Shiel. The Journal expected them to refuse the declaration of office, after which the seats would be declared vacant; whether they did is not recorded here. First names are those of the eight members returned for the West Ward at the January 1920 election (the same eight surnames). Deemed re-elected (no nomination)."
